 See the [API reference documentation](https://docs.page/invertase/denque/api) for more examples.
 
+Remove matching items while preserving the order of the remaining items:
+
+```js
+const filtered = new Denque([1, 2, 3, 4]);
+const removed = filtered.removeWhere((value, index) => value % 2 === 0);
+// removed === 2
+```
+
+The predicate receives each initially present value and its zero-based index. All
+predicate calls finish before any matching items are removed. If the predicate
+throws, the error is propagated and the queue is left unchanged.
+
