+### `removeWhere(function predicate)` -> `int`
+
+Remove every item for which `predicate(value, index)` returns a truthy value.
+The predicate receives values in logical front-to-back order and the zero-based
+index from before filtering. All predicate calls complete before the queue is
+changed. Returns the number of removed items. If the predicate throws, the error
+is propagated and the queue is left unchanged. A non-function predicate throws
+an `Error`, including when the queue is empty.
+
+```js
+var denque = new Denque([1,2,3,4]);
+denque.removeWhere(function (value) { return value % 2 === 0; }); // 2
+denque.toArray(); // [1,3]
+```
+
+
+
